3.7 Proteomic content evaluation of treated SIS portions
From proteomic results, three basic categories, for tissue remodeling, can be considered: 1) the composition of ECM proteins, with the abundant amount of collagen and fibronectin and a subgroup of cytosolic and membrane proteins, 2) proteins that directly or indirectly induce angiogenesis, and 3) cell adhesion (
Figures 6A–C
). The native composition of the ECM showed a variety of protein components related to the structure of the matrix itself and involved in signaling, in equal amounts in smooth and wrinkled portions.
